1
00:00:00,776 --> 00:00:03,656
(Sheldon:)Under the terms of my roommate
agreement I've had control...

2
00:00:03,821 --> 00:00:07,201
(Sheldon:)...of the thermostat
ever since the sweaty night of '06.

3
00:00:07,991 --> 00:00:11,161
(Howard:)Okay, you were right about Wolverine
and bone claws...

4
00:00:11,328 --> 00:00:13,158
(Howard:)...but you're wrong about the cricket.

5
00:00:13,330 --> 00:00:18,000
(Sheldon:)Howard, don't embarrass yourself.
The science chirps for itself.

6
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:20,880
(Sheldon:)Humorous word play.

7
00:00:21,672 --> 00:00:24,382
(Howard:)No, no. Not this time.
I know insects, my friend.

8
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:28,590
(Howard:)I spent many childhood years capturing
them with nets, putting them in jars...

9
00:00:28,762 --> 00:00:32,102
(Howard:)...sticking pins through them, mounting
them on cardboard with labels...

10
00:00:32,266 --> 00:00:35,306
(Howard:)...identifying the genus and species.

11
00:00:35,519 --> 00:00:37,439
(Howard:)In Latin.

12
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:42,860
(Raj:)Oh. Dude, you are never getting
a shiksa goddess.

13
00:00:46,363 --> 00:00:49,743
(Sheldon:)That is a snowy tree cricket.
Oecanthus fultoni.

14
00:00:49,908 --> 00:00:53,038
(Sheldon:)I was done with Latin by fifth grade.

15
00:00:53,537 --> 00:00:54,617
(Howard:)Okay. Tell you what.

16
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:57,870
(Howard:)I am willing to bet anything
that's an ordinary field cricket.

17
00:00:58,041 --> 00:01:01,671
(Sheldon:)-I can't take your money.
-What's the matter, you chicken?

